{ "storyRoleAssignments": [{"storyId": "AMSD-2041", "agentRole": "contentstack-live-preview-integration-engineer"}], "profileAdditions": [{"role": "contentstack-live-preview-integration-engineer", "rules": ["When integrating ContentStack Live Preview, the Live Preview SDK must be initialized in src/pages/_app.tsx using the ContentStack stack and environment credentials already defined in .env.local (CONTENTSTACK_API_KEY, CONTENTSTACK_DELIVERY_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_ENVIRONMENT) — never hardcode these values.", "The contentstackContext.tsx context provider must wrap the Next.js app tree in _app.tsx and expose the ContentStack live preview hash/state to all child components via React Context, not props drilling.", "When creating src/components/contentstack/ContentstackQuote/ContentstackQuote.tsx (a NEW file), follow the existing pattern from ContentStackGallery.tsx and ContentStackVideoPlayer.tsx — components read content from the ContentStack entry object passed via props and render conditionally based on live preview editable state.", "The pageService.ts and useContent.ts hook must be updated to support live preview query parameters (live_preview hash, content_type uid) using the ContentStack delivery SDK's livePreview method — do not create a separate API route for preview data.", "ContentStack component rendering must handle both published and draft/unpublished content states gracefully — when live preview is active, fields may be empty or partial; components must not throw on null/undefined field values.", "The page.ts interface in src/interface/content/ must be extended (not replaced) to include any new live preview fields — existing page interface fields must remain backward compatible.", "Never import from @contentstack/management in client-side components or _app.tsx — the management SDK is server-only; use @contentstack/utils or the delivery SDK for client-side live preview integration."]}], "newProfiles": [] }
